WEBVTT

00:01.300 --> 00:04.376
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.444 --> 00:07.789
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.857 --> 00:10.933
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.001 --> 00:13.911
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.978 --> 00:17.858
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.926 --> 00:20.802
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.870 --> 00:22.408
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.476 --> 00:23.780
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.031 --> 00:27.471
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.936 --> 00:37.779
Everyone, we need to discuss
our problem with Chris.

00:37.819 --> 00:40.377
His little habit of,
uh, personal amusement

00:40.446 --> 00:42.150
is getting way out of hand.

00:42.202 --> 00:43.355
I mean, look at this.

00:43.423 --> 00:44.827
What's that,
some kind of board?

00:44.895 --> 00:46.331
It's Chris' blanket.

00:47.722 --> 00:49.828
We got to do
something about this.

00:49.896 --> 00:52.371
I'm pretty sure our washing
machine is pregnant.

00:52.439 --> 00:54.595
I don't even know how that's
scientifically possible.

00:54.663 --> 00:57.706
Uh, life, uh, uh,
uh, uh, uh, uh...

00:57.775 --> 00:59.162
finds a way.

00:59.230 --> 01:01.671
You know, maybe you guys
should help find Chris a hobby.

01:01.739 --> 01:03.378
Wait a minute, Brian,
that's a great idea.

01:03.445 --> 01:04.447
Chris needs a hobby.

01:04.515 --> 01:05.668
Hey, Chris, get in here.

01:05.736 --> 01:06.872
Yeah, Dad?

01:06.941 --> 01:08.546
We are gonna
find you a hobby.

01:08.614 --> 01:10.418
What do you think of that?
Okay.

01:10.487 --> 01:11.624
There you go,
that's the spirit.

01:13.849 --> 01:15.104
Yuck.

01:18.081 --> 01:20.740
Hey, Christopher.
What you up to?

01:20.808 --> 01:22.396
Hi, Mr. Herbert.

01:22.463 --> 01:24.637
My dad's helping me
find a hobby.

01:24.705 --> 01:27.013
Well, you sure got a
pretty morning for it.

01:27.064 --> 01:28.969
Chris, don't waste
our time with the elderly.

01:29.037 --> 01:30.759
They're dying.

01:33.169 --> 01:36.647
Please, God,
let me just sniff his hat.

01:36.716 --> 01:39.591
Let me just sniff his hat,
that's all I want.

01:42.620 --> 01:44.292
(sniffs)

01:44.360 --> 01:47.303
Now I want more.

01:50.581 --> 01:53.692
Okay, Chris, this is the
gentle art of philately,

01:53.760 --> 01:55.900
otherwise known as
stamp collecting.

01:55.968 --> 01:57.371
Here's a pile of stamps,

01:57.440 --> 02:00.266
carefully culled from swap
meets and garage sales.

02:00.317 --> 02:01.754
And look at this.

02:01.822 --> 02:03.260
It's a Bolivian airplane.

02:03.329 --> 02:06.220
Now, it says it's worth
eight cents, but really...

02:06.289 --> 02:07.978
it's worth 12.

02:08.045 --> 02:10.017
See that? Already ahead.

02:10.102 --> 02:12.527
Came right out of the blocks
with a winner here, Chris.

02:12.594 --> 02:16.642
Now, we'll just paste this very
carefully into the book.

02:16.709 --> 02:19.068
And that's where it belongs.

02:19.135 --> 02:21.057
Now this is a
loaded handgun.

02:21.126 --> 02:23.333
And what we're gonna do
now is kill ourselves

02:23.401 --> 02:24.771
because this is horrible.

02:24.838 --> 02:26.376
Couldn't we just stop
philateling?

02:26.444 --> 02:28.050
Too late.
(gunshot)

02:31.396 --> 02:33.268
All right, Chris, this is
one of the oldest hobbies

02:33.336 --> 02:35.895
in existence: drinking.

02:35.963 --> 02:38.505
Hey, hey, good times
just walked in.

02:38.572 --> 02:40.477
(applause and cheering)

02:40.546 --> 02:42.787
HORACE: Oh, hey, he can't be in here.
He's not 21.

02:42.854 --> 02:45.127
All right, just hang out here
for a little bit, huh?

02:48.106 --> 02:49.912
(slurring words): All right,
see you later, gang.

02:49.979 --> 02:52.120
Chris, what are
you doing here?

02:52.188 --> 02:54.026
You're supposed
to be at camp.

02:54.095 --> 02:56.602
What am I paying for?

02:56.671 --> 03:00.316
I could have gone pro
if it wasn't for my bum knee.

03:00.384 --> 03:02.825
(snoring)

03:02.893 --> 03:05.802
(sighs)

03:05.870 --> 03:07.409
(gasps)
Wow!

03:15.790 --> 03:17.495
That is so cool. What is it?

03:17.562 --> 03:19.301
MAN (with German accent):
It's a puppet.

03:19.369 --> 03:20.923
Welcome.

03:20.975 --> 03:23.851
I am Franz Gutentag,
and this is my puppet shop.

03:23.919 --> 03:25.256
Puppets.

03:25.323 --> 03:26.528
And I thought I'd
seen everything.

03:26.595 --> 03:27.933
My name is Chris.

03:28.001 --> 03:31.128
Well, Chris, puppetry
is a wonderful art form.

03:31.195 --> 03:33.419
You can create an entire world
right before your eyes

03:33.487 --> 03:35.092
and watch it come to life.

03:35.160 --> 03:36.714
Wow.

03:36.782 --> 03:37.985
What's that one
over there?

03:38.053 --> 03:41.147
Ah. That is a work in progress.

03:41.215 --> 03:44.275
It is waiting to become
anything we wish it to be.

03:49.879 --> 03:52.304
My name is Chris,

03:52.371 --> 03:55.215
and I like candy and jumping
and colorful birds.

03:55.282 --> 03:57.556
Wow! What else do I like?

03:57.624 --> 03:59.563
You like the pop singing
of today.

03:59.632 --> 04:01.738
(synthesized pop music playing)

04:01.789 --> 04:03.628
♪ Two, three,
ich berleg' bei mir ♪

04:03.713 --> 04:06.355
♪ Ihr' nas'n spricht daf
whrenddessen ich noch rauch' ♪

04:06.423 --> 04:08.462
♪ Die special places
sind ihr wohlbekannt ♪

04:08.530 --> 04:09.867
♪ Ich mein', sie fhrt
ja u-bahn auch ♪

04:09.935 --> 04:11.774
♪ Dort singen's dreh'
dich nicht, um ♪

04:11.842 --> 04:13.496
♪ Ooh, oh, oh ♪

04:13.582 --> 04:14.718
♪ Schau, schau ♪

04:14.786 --> 04:16.056
♪ Der kommissar geht, um ♪

04:16.125 --> 04:18.097
♪ Ooh, oh, oh. ♪

04:18.148 --> 04:19.653
Yay!

04:19.721 --> 04:22.530
That was the German-est
thing I've ever seen.

04:22.598 --> 04:24.336
I'm so glad
you like it, Chris.

04:24.404 --> 04:25.909
Would you like to try?

04:25.977 --> 04:27.314
Oh, boy, would I?!

04:30.058 --> 04:34.289
I'm a vampire, and I'm in love
with this unattractive girl.

04:34.358 --> 04:36.681
Grr, I'm a werewolf,

04:36.748 --> 04:39.391
and I am also in love
with this unattractive girl.

04:39.459 --> 04:42.669
Boy, she sure can act though, can't she?
Nope.

04:42.737 --> 04:45.211
The end.
(laughing)

04:45.279 --> 04:46.784
Bravo, Chris!

04:46.852 --> 04:48.256
You have really
tapped into

04:48.324 --> 04:50.347
the wonder and enchantment
that is puppetry.

04:50.415 --> 04:53.273
Plus I move these dolls and
make like they're talking.

04:53.342 --> 04:54.579
Yes. Right.

04:54.647 --> 04:56.652
Thanks for showing
me how to do it

04:56.721 --> 04:58.727
and being so nice to
me, Mr. Gutentag.

04:58.795 --> 05:00.249
Call me Franz.

05:00.317 --> 05:02.324
Okay. Franz.

05:02.392 --> 05:04.783
You know, Chris,
seeing a young person like you

05:04.850 --> 05:07.158
enjoy puppetry
makes me so happy.

05:07.242 --> 05:09.667
I feel like we could
become good friends.

05:09.735 --> 05:11.942
That sounds like fun.

05:12.010 --> 05:14.384
Wow, I think you're just
about my most favorite guy

05:14.451 --> 05:16.023
who's gonna die soon.

05:16.090 --> 05:19.903
That's the nicest thing
anyone has ever said to me.

05:19.971 --> 05:22.463
Oh, no!

05:26.573 --> 05:27.943
(knocking on door)

05:29.182 --> 05:31.440
Mr. Griffin,
I'm sorry to bother you,

05:31.510 --> 05:32.881
but there's a...

05:32.939 --> 05:35.264
Well, there's a situation,
and we need to talk.

05:35.332 --> 05:37.606
Look, if this is about those
droppings in your yard,

05:37.674 --> 05:39.312
it was, uh, uh, Brian.

05:39.379 --> 05:40.750
Yeah, Brian.

05:40.818 --> 05:43.059
No, it's this man Chris
is hanging out with.

05:43.127 --> 05:44.798
He's bad news.

05:44.849 --> 05:46.706
Why? What's
the problem?

05:46.773 --> 05:49.984
Chris is friends with a Nazi!
What?!

05:50.052 --> 05:51.924
At first I wasn't sure
it was him,

05:51.992 --> 05:56.574
but I got a closer look, and now
there's no question in my mind.

05:56.642 --> 05:58.882
Franz Gutentag is really

05:58.951 --> 06:02.964
Lieutenant Franz Schlechtnacht,
the most sadistic S.S. guard

06:03.032 --> 06:05.640
in all of Hitler's
concentration camps.

06:05.709 --> 06:08.417
That's a very
serious accusation.

06:08.484 --> 06:11.093
How do you know this man
was a Nazi prison guard?

06:11.144 --> 06:13.486
'Cause I was there.

06:13.570 --> 06:16.780
<i>It was 1944.</i>

06:16.831 --> 06:20.093
<i>I was a young Air Force pilot
assigned as part of an escort</i>

06:20.144 --> 06:22.401
<i>for a bombing raid
over southern Germany,</i>

06:22.468 --> 06:24.943
<i>when we encountered
the Luftwaffe.</i>

06:26.601 --> 06:28.757
<i>At first we thought
we were in the clear</i>

06:28.824 --> 06:30.547
<i>because the Germans
were frightened</i>

06:30.632 --> 06:33.441
<i>by the scary shark face
on the front of our plane.</i>

06:33.508 --> 06:34.679
Ah! A shark!

06:34.746 --> 06:36.836
How did it get all the way
up here in the sky?!

06:36.903 --> 06:38.326
Who cares, you fool?!

06:38.393 --> 06:39.998
Do you want to get
eaten? Retreat!

06:43.060 --> 06:45.568
<i>But there was one
stubborn pilot</i>

06:45.653 --> 06:47.073
<i>who saw through our disguise.</i>

06:49.701 --> 06:51.038
(machine guns firing)

07:12.483 --> 07:17.785
<i>Most of the surviving American
pilots were taken to POW camps,</i>

07:17.852 --> 07:20.109
<i>but for some reason,
they thought I was gay,</i>

07:20.177 --> 07:22.903
<i>so I was taken
to a concentration camp.</i>

07:22.987 --> 07:26.031
<i>Behind those walls,</i>

07:26.082 --> 07:29.912
<i>there was one guard
who decided everyone's fate.</i>

07:29.980 --> 07:33.591
<i>If he pointed to the left,
you did hard labor.</i>

07:33.660 --> 07:37.205
<i>If he pointed to the right,
you died.</i>

07:37.256 --> 07:40.382
<i>That man was
Franz Schlechtnacht.</i>

07:40.434 --> 07:44.782
<i>I was spared death,
but I was given hard labor.</i>

07:44.850 --> 07:47.408
<i>He made me sort
the camp recyclables.</i>

07:47.475 --> 07:49.014
<i>But some of those bottles</i>

07:49.082 --> 07:51.088
<i>still had a little bit
of soda in 'em.</i>

07:51.156 --> 07:54.400
<i>It would spill out on my hands
and make 'em kind of sticky.</i>

07:54.468 --> 07:56.440
<i>Dear God, how my hands</i>

07:56.492 --> 07:58.448
<i>would get kind of sticky!</i>

07:58.499 --> 08:00.505
(screaming)

08:00.590 --> 08:03.499
(evil laughter)

08:03.567 --> 08:07.096
<i>No one should have to suffer
the way I suffered!</i>

08:07.164 --> 08:11.010
So that's why Chris should stay
away from that puppet store guy.

08:11.078 --> 08:12.583
That all sounds
kind of sketchy.

08:12.651 --> 08:14.154
Wait, are you
Jamie Kennedy?

08:14.223 --> 08:16.463
Am I... am I being skunked

08:16.531 --> 08:18.002
or puked or whatever
some (bleep)?

08:18.070 --> 08:20.075
I'm telling you the truth.

08:20.144 --> 08:22.385
I swear on my nephew's grave.

08:22.452 --> 08:25.329
I don't know, Franz seems
like such a nice old man.

08:25.397 --> 08:27.937
Y-You know, maybe we should
just invite him for dinner

08:28.005 --> 08:29.343
and clear this
whole thing up.

08:29.411 --> 08:31.517
Yeah, you know, we got
no right passing judgment

08:31.585 --> 08:32.890
without getting to know him.

08:32.957 --> 08:34.361
Isn't that right,
Scottish Chipmunk?

08:36.134 --> 08:38.709
Yeah, he doesn't talk,
but, uh, he's a chipmunk,

08:38.778 --> 08:41.520
and he's Scottish, and he
would back me up on this.

08:45.954 --> 08:47.909
Chris, wait.
Where you going?

08:47.977 --> 08:50.419
I'm going to
Mr. Gutentag's house.

08:50.487 --> 08:51.857
You can't.
Why not?

08:51.925 --> 08:54.801
Chris, his name
isn't Gutentag,

08:54.870 --> 08:57.344
it's Schlechtnacht,
and he's a Nazi.

08:57.412 --> 08:58.649
What?!

08:58.717 --> 09:00.322
It's true.

09:00.390 --> 09:02.530
You got to stay away
from that terrible man.

09:02.597 --> 09:04.905
Mr. Gutentag
isn't a terrible man.

09:04.973 --> 09:06.845
He's my friend.

09:06.913 --> 09:10.023
Chris, you don't understand,
I'm trying to help you.

09:10.091 --> 09:11.227
Help me what?

09:11.295 --> 09:13.168
Clean your pool
with my shirt off,

09:13.236 --> 09:14.506
or wash your car
in jean shorts,

09:14.574 --> 09:16.179
bend over in front of you

09:16.247 --> 09:18.353
to get little bits
of lint out of the rug?

09:18.421 --> 09:20.193
I know what you're about,
Mr. Herbert:

09:20.262 --> 09:23.171
free labor,
and I'm not into it.

09:23.239 --> 09:25.981
Chris, you have to choose.

09:26.048 --> 09:28.122
It's either Franz or me.

09:37.874 --> 09:40.383
Chris, what's the matter?
You look upset.

09:40.451 --> 09:43.728
Mr. Herbert was saying
terrible things about you.

09:43.795 --> 09:47.107
He said you liked Hitler, and
your name isn't really Gutentag.

09:47.174 --> 09:50.854
Oh, Chris, you can't always
believe what you hear.

09:50.921 --> 09:53.998
For example, everybody thinks
that prostitution is illegal,

09:54.067 --> 09:55.604
but there are ways around it.

09:55.671 --> 09:57.913
All right, let's do it.

09:57.964 --> 10:00.255
Both of you are under
arrest for prostitution.

10:00.322 --> 10:01.626
It's not
prostitution.

10:01.694 --> 10:03.533
You paid her
to have sex.

10:03.600 --> 10:06.343
No, I paid her to have sex
and we're filming it.

10:06.411 --> 10:08.785
So, technically it's not
prostitution, it's a porno.

10:08.854 --> 10:10.424
Oh, well,

10:10.492 --> 10:12.332
as long as you're filming
and selling it, it's legal.

10:12.400 --> 10:13.971
Enjoy your day.

10:14.039 --> 10:17.317
Remember kids, she's not
a whore if she's an actress.

10:17.384 --> 10:21.063
<i>ANNOUNCER:
This has been a message from:</i>

10:21.132 --> 10:22.602
(knocking on door)

10:22.669 --> 10:25.429
Oh, that's probably
mean old Mr. Herbert again.

10:25.497 --> 10:26.850
Dad?
Excuse me, Chris,

10:26.901 --> 10:28.775
I got to talk to
Mr. Pupenchest here.

10:28.843 --> 10:30.414
Good day to you,
Mr. Griffin.

10:30.482 --> 10:32.789
Say, listen, my wife and I
appreciate how nice you've been

10:32.857 --> 10:34.729
to my son with all
the puppets and whatnot,

10:34.797 --> 10:36.787
and, uh, we wanted
to invite you over for dinner.

10:36.855 --> 10:38.258
Oh, wonderful.

10:38.326 --> 10:40.065
And I shall celebrate
our friendship

10:40.134 --> 10:42.675
by giving you a hand-carved
German wall clock.

10:42.742 --> 10:44.247
Oh, yes, yes,
yes, yes, yes.

10:46.288 --> 10:47.659
I could not
find the clock.

10:47.727 --> 10:49.198
Aw.

10:49.266 --> 10:51.172
But you got three of them
on the wall over there.

10:51.240 --> 10:52.611
Yes, those are mine.

10:52.678 --> 10:54.350
Oh.

10:54.417 --> 10:55.454
Yeah, I need those.

10:55.521 --> 10:57.060
Uh-huh.

10:57.128 --> 10:59.066
I just don't know why
you said it then.

10:59.134 --> 11:01.643
Mr. Gutentag,
can I use the bathroom?

11:01.711 --> 11:03.584
Of course. Down the
hall to the right.

11:03.652 --> 11:05.156
It's the door marked:

11:05.224 --> 11:08.384
<i>"gluckmachnichten-
mechwerchtichlieber."</i>

11:20.830 --> 11:22.150
What the...?

11:35.248 --> 11:38.057
So now you know
the truth.

11:39.866 --> 11:42.272
I promise I won't tell anyone!

11:42.341 --> 11:44.715
Just let my dad go!

11:44.783 --> 11:48.362
Oh, I am afraid that
is quite impossible.

11:53.163 --> 11:55.270
You're not gonna get away
with this, Mr. Googlesearch.

11:55.338 --> 11:57.529
Oh, but I think that I will.

11:57.613 --> 11:59.100
You two know my secret.

11:59.168 --> 12:02.044
I must be sure no one
ever finds out the truth.

12:02.112 --> 12:03.717
So what? Are you gonna kill us?

12:03.785 --> 12:05.557
Perhaps, Mr. Griffin.

12:05.625 --> 12:07.364
I have not yet decided.

12:07.432 --> 12:09.572
Well, you might want to do
something about that first.

12:09.773 --> 12:10.874
What?

12:13.253 --> 12:15.159
Quick, shoot him, Chris!
What are you waiting for?!

12:15.227 --> 12:17.434
I-I... How do I know
which one to shoot?

12:17.501 --> 12:18.135
What?

12:18.203 --> 12:19.241
How do I know

12:19.308 --> 12:20.612
which one is the real dad?!

12:20.679 --> 12:22.569
I... we-we never switched.

12:22.636 --> 12:23.840
We don't even look the same!

12:23.908 --> 12:25.446
All right, when's my birthday?

12:25.514 --> 12:26.784
Ah, crap.

12:26.851 --> 12:27.721
February eighth.

12:28.592 --> 12:29.610
(gasps)

12:29.679 --> 12:30.681
Dad!

12:33.978 --> 12:35.582
There. That's
more like it.

12:35.651 --> 12:36.988
You idiot!

12:37.055 --> 12:39.664
Well, learn my birthday,
(bleep)!

12:46.962 --> 12:49.302
Mrs. Griffin!
What a nice surprise!

12:49.370 --> 12:50.440
Come in!

12:50.508 --> 12:53.083
Mr. Gutentag,
I'm sorry to bother you,

12:53.151 --> 12:56.294
but Chris and Peter
didn't come home last night.

12:56.363 --> 12:57.565
Have you seen them?

12:57.634 --> 13:00.476
Oh, wait, is he a
great big fat person?

13:00.545 --> 13:02.449
He's a large man,
yes, sir.

13:02.517 --> 13:04.056
No, I have not seen them.

13:04.124 --> 13:06.130
Well, if you do,
could you please contact me?

13:06.198 --> 13:08.103
I'm just worried sick.

13:08.172 --> 13:09.709
Of course,
Mrs. Griffin.

13:09.777 --> 13:12.052
I will let you
know immediately.

13:12.136 --> 13:13.707
Dad, I want to go home.

13:13.775 --> 13:16.317
All right, let's try
and figure a way outta here.

13:16.385 --> 13:18.056
Look around.
See if you can find something

13:18.124 --> 13:19.511
to break the door down with.

13:21.068 --> 13:24.263
(gasps)
Dad, there's a window here!

13:24.330 --> 13:26.085
Oh, my God,
maybe we can get outside.

13:26.153 --> 13:29.063
No, it's too small.

13:29.130 --> 13:30.668
Wait, Dad, look.

13:30.737 --> 13:33.144
There's Meg walking down
the street.

13:35.454 --> 13:36.624
Hey, Meg!

13:36.691 --> 13:38.396
Hanging out with
all your friends?

13:38.464 --> 13:39.936
(both laugh)

13:39.987 --> 13:43.281
Hey, whale,
the ocean's that way!

13:43.333 --> 13:44.536
That's a good one, too.

13:44.603 --> 13:46.677
All right, let's figure
a way to get outta here.

13:46.745 --> 13:48.215
Now we can't fit
through the window,

13:48.283 --> 13:50.055
but maybe there's
some way we can let

13:50.123 --> 13:51.377
people know
we're down here.

13:51.445 --> 13:52.948
We gotta make
as much noise as possible

13:53.017 --> 13:54.387
to get people's attention.

13:54.455 --> 13:58.000
And nothing makes more noise
than unwanted salsa music.

13:58.069 --> 13:59.539
Hand me that radio.

14:01.564 --> 14:03.822
(loud salsa music plays)

14:05.010 --> 14:06.582
(loud salsa music continues)

14:06.667 --> 14:08.538
What the hell?

14:08.606 --> 14:11.316
Oh, for God's sake, where's
that white noise machine?

14:12.889 --> 14:14.628
(woman screams)

14:14.696 --> 14:15.966
Help!

14:16.033 --> 14:17.872
Oh, my God, help!

14:17.940 --> 14:19.010
Somebody help me!

14:19.078 --> 14:21.920
(sighs)

14:21.988 --> 14:24.446
(music turns to static)

14:24.514 --> 14:26.856
Aw, man,
the battery's dead.

14:26.940 --> 14:28.243
Now what do we do?

14:28.311 --> 14:30.032
(gasp)
Oh, my God.

14:31.740 --> 14:34.164
Mr. Herbert! Mr. Herbert!

14:35.922 --> 14:37.743
Oh, he can't hear me.

14:37.811 --> 14:40.354
Jesse! Jesse!

14:40.405 --> 14:42.126
(barks weakly)

14:42.194 --> 14:45.171
Jesse, what is it, boy?

14:45.222 --> 14:47.145
(gasps)
Chris!

14:47.213 --> 14:49.051
Chris, what happened?!

14:49.119 --> 14:50.641
You were right, Mr. Herbert.

14:50.709 --> 14:52.146
<i>Franz is a Nazi.</i>

14:52.215 --> 14:53.651
And he's keeping us prisoner
down here.

14:53.719 --> 14:54.923
Get help.

14:54.991 --> 14:56.964
Oh, and if you
see Meg, tell her

14:57.031 --> 14:58.637
"Thunder Thighs
are on the move!

14:58.705 --> 14:59.908
Thunder Thighs
are loose."

14:59.976 --> 15:01.864
You know, I gotta say, Chris,

15:01.932 --> 15:05.076
all my life I wanted
to see you locked in a basement,

15:05.127 --> 15:09.224
but now that it's happened,
all I want to do is get you out.

15:09.292 --> 15:13.423
Don't you worry.
I'll be back with help.

15:13.491 --> 15:15.263
You want me to write that Thunder
Thighs thing down for you?

15:15.331 --> 15:16.668
Ah, he's not gonna do it.

15:43.834 --> 15:45.722
I'm here for the boy.

15:45.774 --> 15:46.760
Who are you?

15:46.812 --> 15:48.985
Oh, you don't remember me?

15:49.052 --> 15:52.531
Well, I remember you,
Lieutenant Schlechtnacht.

15:52.598 --> 15:53.735
(gasps)

15:53.803 --> 15:55.676
<i>But then why should you
remember?</i>

15:55.744 --> 15:57.615
There were so many of us.

15:57.683 --> 15:59.991
But, frankly,
I don't give a damn.

16:00.059 --> 16:01.630
And I'll tell you this:

16:01.698 --> 16:05.444
only one of us is gonna
walk outta here alive.

16:07.352 --> 16:08.940
Bring it on!

16:09.007 --> 16:10.647
(dramatic action music plays)

16:41.475 --> 16:43.381
♪ ♪

17:13.022 --> 17:14.862
♪ ♪

17:27.977 --> 17:31.371
(snoring)

17:31.439 --> 17:33.413
Wake up. Wake up.
We're fighting.

17:33.481 --> 17:35.520
Wh-where-where am I?

17:35.588 --> 17:37.008
It's okay.
We're fighting.

17:37.075 --> 17:38.213
Wake up.

17:38.281 --> 17:40.120
♪ ♪

18:05.429 --> 18:07.803
(rapid beeping)

18:10.614 --> 18:12.721
Uh, hang on.
Hang on. Pills.

18:12.788 --> 18:14.678
Yeah, me, too.

18:19.062 --> 18:20.532
Wednesday, right?

18:20.599 --> 18:22.540
Yeah, it's Wednesday.

18:32.660 --> 18:34.249
Uh, you know what?
You know what?

18:34.333 --> 18:36.022
What?

18:36.089 --> 18:37.762
I'm having some trouble
getting up.

18:37.829 --> 18:38.999
Would you mind
calling my nurse?

18:39.067 --> 18:40.237
Her name is Frieda.

18:40.304 --> 18:42.612
Her phone number
is in the kitchen.

18:52.615 --> 18:54.421
(dramatic action music playing)

18:54.489 --> 18:56.278
(singsongy):
Oh, gosh,

18:56.346 --> 18:58.318
look who's stuck
on the couch again.

18:58.387 --> 18:59.757
I'm not stuck on the couch.

18:59.825 --> 19:01.296
Okay, Mr. Cranky.

19:01.348 --> 19:03.421
One, two...

19:03.489 --> 19:04.607
three!

19:04.675 --> 19:05.779
There we go!

19:05.847 --> 19:08.254
You didn't need me.
You did that yourself.

19:08.322 --> 19:10.111
Good for you.

19:10.179 --> 19:11.517
You need anything else?

19:11.584 --> 19:13.323
No, I'm fine, thank you.

19:13.391 --> 19:16.032
Okay, you guys have fun.

19:43.717 --> 19:45.489
♪ ♪

20:01.482 --> 20:04.123
Franz, grab my hand!

20:06.215 --> 20:08.724
(mournful music plays)

20:27.241 --> 20:29.966
(bones cracking)

20:33.280 --> 20:36.858
Say good night,
you Nazi bastard.

20:36.943 --> 20:40.806
(birds chirping)

20:40.874 --> 20:42.545
Thanks for everything,
Mr. Herbert.

20:42.613 --> 20:44.520
If only I had
listened to you,

20:44.588 --> 20:45.824
none of this
would've happened.

20:45.892 --> 20:47.730
You were my real
friend all along.

20:47.798 --> 20:49.370
I'm sorry.

20:49.438 --> 20:50.876
It's okay, Chris.

20:50.943 --> 20:54.388
Sometimes the only way to really
appreciate what you have

20:54.456 --> 20:56.831
is to see what life is like
without it.

20:56.899 --> 21:00.611
And there's nothing I appreciate
more than your friendship.

21:07.353 --> 21:10.011
Dad, Mr. Herbert called
me "Thunder Thighs."

21:10.079 --> 21:12.421
Oh, you did it.
Thank you.

21:12.422 --> 22:13.422
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru